  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/embedded-content.html#the-video-element\n\n> When no video data is available (the element's readyState attribute is either HAVE_NOTHING, or HAVE_METADATA but no video data has yet been obtained at all, or the element's readyState attribute is any subsequent value but the media resource does not have a video channel)\n> The video element represents its poster frame, if any, or else transparent black with no intrinsic dimensions.\n\nIt looks like this has been written without taking into account the possibility that there is a thumbnail/preview/cover picture in the metadata.\n\nThis should be changed to something like (better phrased of course):\n\n> When no video data is available (...):\n> - if the video has a poster frame, the video element presents it\n> - otherwise, if the status is HAVE_METADATA and a preview image is present in the metadata, the video element presents it [something like that]\n> - otherwise, transparent black with no intrinsic dimensions.\n",
